# Zurgo protects Warrior tokens only during its controller's own end step (CR 604.1, 613.1f, 701.21a; "During your end step").
# The two mobilized Warriors outlive Bot1's end step, mobilize's sacrifice doing nothing to them; in Bot2's end step on the next
# turn Zurgo gives them nothing, so Bot1's Ashnod's Altar sacrifices one, and the other is still there.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Zurgo, Thunder's Decree
Black Lotus
Ashnod's Altar
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Zurgo, Thunder's Decree.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Ashnod's Altar.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Zurgo, Thunder's Decree > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token#2.Colors = Red
[T4 Bot2.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ashnod's Altar.Activate(Sacrifice: Warrior Token#1)

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield = Ashnod's Altar; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Warrior Token; Zurgo, Thunder's Decree
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
